WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.967
Change the wording of an email or text.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:11.367
Start from a card. Every automation card has its own wording (the Wording button at the top opens the same place).

00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:16.833
Edit wording. Opens that message. Here: the appointment reminder.

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:23.600
The message. Its name, and when it was last changed and by whom ("Standard wording" if never).

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:30.633
Send it. Switches this one message off without stopping its automation. Kept when you press Save wording.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:35.800
Subject. The email's subject line. {placeholders} work here too.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:43.267
Message. The email text. A blank line starts a new paragraph. The preview follows as you type.

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:53.233
Placeholders. Click one to put it where the cursor is: first name, appointment day and time, who with, address… Each customer gets their own.

00:00:53.733 --> 00:01:03.200
Text message version. The text version, sent only when texts are switched on. Keep it under 160 characters; the hint counts them.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:11.833
Preview. Below: the message as a real customer would get it, with sample numbers. It follows your changes as you type.

00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:16.300
Save wording. Keeps it; the next messages use it.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.533
Undo changes. Goes back to the saved wording.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:32.467
Every message. Every message the system sends, including some with no switch of their own (You're on the schedule, the yearly maintenance price change). "Off" marks one switched off.

00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:36.367
Pick another one. Click a message to change it.

00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:43.167
Button. A message with a link has a button; this is its wording, e.g. View your estimate.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:49.267
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
